      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-116128",
      ":question/problem": "The intensity $I$ of the sound in an auditorium, measured in decibels $(dB)$, is inversely proportional to the **square** of the distance $d$, measured in meters, between the sound source and the people listening. A device that measures sound intensity is $8$ meters from the source and registers $25$ $dB$. What equation gives the relationship between $I$ and $d$?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
